  "comment": "kiln.labbot (lab servers only): bot players the dedicated server hosts itself. The session publishes its machines and players to the GameServer in a double-buffered state (session +0x3c the published buffer, +0x48 the two 0x2668-byte buffers; players at +0x178, 16 x 0x150; machines at +0x1678, 17 x 0xf0); SessionPublish(session, buffer) makes a filled back buffer current, so a bot added to it there is seen by every reader. The join then calls the game's own receive handlers, as ServerReceive does for a client: AddPlayer (machine channel 0, Login), Save2Receive (player save channel, the character upload, acks and the final request) and net/MachineLogin (SystemsReady, GameplayReady). Evidence: docs/re/labbot.md (server f0d824be, svn 1287369).",
